// Stories at three scales, meant to chain together and to hang off real features of the world.
//   BIG:    world arcs { id, n, req?: world condition, d, signs: [local templates], stages: [...],
//           links: { tags: [realm/province tags], sites: [MYST names], factions: [realm tags] },
//           slots?: [premise slots it occupies; dropped when an active premise fills one],
//           soft?: [those of its slots where it survives as stage-0 rumour instead],
//           absorbedBy?: [premise ids that keep it at full strength as their visible arc] }.
//           At most one BIG with "apocalypse" in slots per world. d/n/stages are shown raw; signs are filled.
//           World tags: has:titans has:rifts has:ley has:node has:breach has:ruins has:volcanoes has:wars
//           has:fallen_empire has:void_faith has:titan_faith magic:high magic:low wild:high many_islands,
//           premise:<id> slot:<slot> tone:<tone> genre:<genre> default:power default:cosmos.
//           has:ley only under default:power, has:rifts only under default:cosmos (node/breach always).
//   MEDIUM: realm/regional arcs { id, n, scope, req?: realm condition, d, links: [BIG ids], hooks: [...] }.
//   SMALL:  local hooks { id, t, where, req?: province condition, links?: [MEDIUM or BIG ids] }.
// Conditions follow rules.js (tag, "!tag", [all], {any}, {not}). Slots in {braces} are filled at
// generation time; see the header of each list for the slots it may use. Keep every template 1-3 sentences.

